IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nha-indexation`

-- National Health Act 1953, ss 99F, 99G -- worked cases for nha-indexation.l4.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand from the
-- text and the s 99G(3)-(4) formulas before running. The CPI numbers are ILLUSTRATIVE (September 2025 to 2029: 140, 144.2, 146,
-- 145, 150), and the known figures are the printed $25.00 and $1,457.10 and an illustrative $7.70 concessional charge, taken as in
-- force from 1 January 2026. None of the results is an amount in force.

`illustrative September CPI` MEANS LIST 140, 144.2, 146, 145, 150

§ `s 99G(4)-(7) -- the factor`

-- 144.2 / 140 = 1.03. 146 / 144.2 = 1.01248: 1.012 (the 4th place 4). 145 / 146: below 1, so 1.
#ASSERT `What is the PBS indexation factor` 144.2 140 EQUALS 1.03
#ASSERT `What is the PBS indexation factor` 146 144.2 EQUALS 1.012
#ASSERT `What is the PBS indexation factor` 145 146 EQUALS 1

§ `s 99G(1), (3) -- one indexation day`

-- $25.00 x 1.03 = $25.75, a multiple of 5 cents: increased by 5 cents to $25.80.
#ASSERT `What does the PBS amount become on 1 January` `the general patient charge` 2027 25 144.2 140 EQUALS 25.8
-- The general patient charge is not indexed on 1 January 2026 (s 99G(1A)); the concessional charge not on 1 January 2027 (1B).
#ASSERT `What does the PBS amount become on 1 January` `the general patient charge` 2026 25 144.2 140 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `What does the PBS amount become on 1 January` `the concessional beneficiary charge` 2027 7.7 144.2 140 EQUALS 7.7

§ `s 99G -- the amount in force from a known figure`

-- General patient charge from $25.00 (2026): 2027 $25.80; 2028 $25.80 x 1.012 = $26.1096, $26.10; 2029 factor 1, $26.10.
#ASSERT `What is the PBS amount in force from 1 January` `the general patient charge` 25 2026 2027 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS JUST 25.8
#ASSERT `What is the PBS amount in force from 1 January` `the general patient charge` 25 2026 2028 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS JUST 26.1
#ASSERT `What is the PBS amount in force from 1 January` `the general patient charge` 25 2026 2029 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS JUST 26.1
-- 2030: $26.10 x 1.034 (150 / 145 = 1.03448) = $26.9874, $27.00. 2031 needs September 2030, not supplied: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the PBS amount in force from 1 January` `the general patient charge` 25 2026 2030 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS JUST 27
#ASSERT `What is the PBS amount in force from 1 January` `the general patient charge` 25 2026 2031 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The general patient safety net, $1,457.10 x 1.03 = $1,500.813, to $1,500.80 on 1 January 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the PBS amount in force from 1 January` `the general patient safety net` 1457.10 2026 2027 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS JUST 1500.8
-- The concessional charge is frozen 2027-2029, so $7.70 until 1 January 2030: $7.70 x 1.034 = $7.9618, $8.00.
#ASSERT `What is the PBS amount in force from 1 January` `the concessional beneficiary charge` 7.7 2026 2029 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS JUST 7.7
#ASSERT `What is the PBS amount in force from 1 January` `the concessional beneficiary charge` 7.7 2026 2030 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS JUST 8

§ `s 99F -- the concessional safety net follows the charge`

-- 36 x $7.70 = $277.20 in 2028; 36 x $8.00 = $288 in 2030.
#ASSERT `What is the concessional safety net from 1 January` 7.7 2026 2028 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS JUST 277.2
#ASSERT `What is the concessional safety net from 1 January` 7.7 2026 2030 `illustrative September CPI` EQUALS JUST 288
